WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.462
A narrow field contract does not determine
which record a caller may change.

2
00:00:04.542 --> 00:00:07.947
Enforce object-level scope with tenant,
owner, administrator,

3
00:00:08.027 --> 00:00:09.389
and current-state rules.

4
00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:13.679
Prefer scoped lookups or updates that
include the security boundary in the query

5
00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:17.721
where appropriate, then apply field-level
permission and business logic.

6
00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:22.135
An authenticated principal can still be
unauthorized for the target object or for a

7
00:00:22.215 --> 00:00:23.825
particular field transition.

8
00:00:23.905 --> 00:00:28.300
Ensure an unscoped object loaded earlier
cannot bypass the tenant condition during

9
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.123
persistence.

10
00:00:29.203 --> 00:00:32.732
Review the complete flow from request
through runtime validation,

11
00:00:32.812 --> 00:00:35.970
authorization, mapping, business logic,
and persistence.

12
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.517
Search for direct req.body usage, object
spread, Object.assign,

13
00:00:39.597 --> 00:00:42.940
generic model binders, Partial of an
entity used as a public DTO,

14
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.991
ORM-generated update inputs in controller
signatures,

15
00:00:46.071 --> 00:00:48.548
nested relation operations, and bulk
updates.

16
00:00:48.628 --> 00:00:52.900
Identify where the writable-field
allowlist is expressed and confirm later code

17
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.527
cannot reintroduce raw data.

18
00:00:54.607 --> 00:00:58.879
Negative tests are especially important
because intended clients never send the

19
00:00:58.959 --> 00:01:00.878
properties that reveal this defect.

20
00:01:00.958 --> 00:01:04.611
Submit unknown keys, server-owned fields,
privileged state fields,

21
00:01:04.691 --> 00:01:08.529
nested unauthorized children, and fields
valid on a different endpoint.

22
00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:12.572
Test another tenant's identifier,
unauthorized administrative actions,

23
00:01:12.652 --> 00:01:16.862
null and omission boundaries, empty
values, duplicate or conflicting changes,

24
00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:20.285
and bulk requests containing at least one
out-of-scope object.

25
00:01:20.365 --> 00:01:23.460
Assert both the response and unchanged
persistence state.

26
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.698
Add regression tests when models gain
columns or relations.

27
00:01:26.778 --> 00:01:30.740
A useful invariant is that the endpoint's
writable set changes only when its

28
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.306
contract and mapper change.

29
00:01:32.386 --> 00:01:36.657
Log denied privileged operations and
authorization failures without recording

30
00:01:36.737 --> 00:01:38.161
sensitive request bodies.

31
00:01:38.241 --> 00:01:42.885
Least-privilege database accounts and
constraints provide containment and invariant

32
00:01:42.965 --> 00:01:47.484
protection, but ordinary database
permissions rarely express field-level business

33
00:01:47.564 --> 00:01:48.678
policy per endpoint.

34
00:01:48.758 --> 00:01:53.216
The application service remains
responsible for translating authenticated intent

35
00:01:53.296 --> 00:01:56.020
into an authorized, explicit persistence
command.
